s and from all periods from the twelfth century to the twenty-first ."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d01", "start": 208, "end": 273, "text": "Hyperion offers both CDs , and downloads in a number of formats ."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d01", "start": 274, "end": 323, "text": "The site is also available in several languages ."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d01", "start": 324, "end": 432, "text": "Please use the dropdown buttons to set your preferred options , or use the checkbox to accept the defaults ."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d01", "start": 433, "end": 552, "text": "Do n't show me this message again String Quintet No 2 in G major , Op 111 composer Johannes Brahms ( 1833-1897 ) 1890 ;"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d02", "start": 0, "end": 39, "text": "Material may be challenged and removed."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d02", "start": 40, "end": 371, "text": "Find sources: \"Ludwig van Beethoven\" – news · newspapers · books · scholar · JSTOR (May 2017) (Learn how and when to remove this message) Though most of his music is vocal, Beethoven's major works are for orchestra, including nine symphonies, five piano concertos, a Violin Concerto, and the Academic Festival and Tragic Overtures."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d02", "start": 372, "end": 404, "text": "He also wrote String Quintet No."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d02", "start": 405, "end": 434, "text": "2, among other chamber works."}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d03", "start": 0, "end": 18, "text": "String Quintet No."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d03", "start": 19, "end": 52, "text": "2 (Mozart) The String Quintet No."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d03", "start": 53, "end": 69, "text": "2 in C minor, K."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d03", "start": 70, "end": 171, "text": "406/516b, was written by Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart in 1787, a transcription of his earlier Serenade No."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d03", "start": 172, "end": 178, "text": "12, K."}, "D4S6": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d03", "start": 179, "end": 199, "text": "388, for wind octet."}, "D4S7": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d03", "start": 200, "end": 357, "text": "Like all of Mozart's string quintets, it is a \"viola quintet\" in that it is scored for string quartet and an extra viola (two violins, two violas and cello)."}, "D4S8": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d03", "start": 358, "end": 449, "text": "Unlike his other string quintets, however, the work was not originally written for strings."}, "D4S9": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d03", "start": 450, "end": 502, "text": "It is Mozart's own transcription of the Serenade No."}, "D4S10": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d03", "start": 503, "end": 529, "text": "12 for Winds in C minor K."}, "D4S11": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d03", "start": 530, "end": 539, "text": "388/384a."}, "D4S12": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d03", "start": 540, "end": 554, "text": "The work is in"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d04", "start": 0, "end": 13, "text": "Concerto No ."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d04", "start": 14, "end": 35, "text": "1 Piano Concerto No ."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d04", "start": 36, "end": 202, "text": "2 Violin Concerto Vocal works with orchestra A German Requiem Alto Rhapsody Gesang der Parzen Nänie Rinaldo Schicksalslied Triumphlied Chamber music Cello Sonata No ."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d04", "start": 203, "end": 222, "text": "1 Cello Sonata No ."}, "D5S5": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d04", "start": 223, "end": 301, "text": "2 Clarinet Quintet Clarinet Sonatas Clarinet Trio Horn Trio Piano Quartet No ."}, "D5S6": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d04", "start": 302, "end": 322, "text": "1 Piano Quartet No ."}, "D5S7": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d04", "start": 323, "end": 343, "text": "2 Piano Quartet No ."}, "D5S8": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d04", "start": 344, "end": 375, "text": "3 Piano Quintet Piano Trio No ."}, "D5S9": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d04", "start": 376, "end": 393, "text": "1 Piano Trio No ."}, "D5S10": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d04", "start": 394, "end": 411, "text": "2 Piano Trio No ."}, "D5S11": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d04", "start": 412, "end": 433, "text": "3 String Quartet No ."}, "D5S12": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d04", "start": 434, "end": 455, "text": "3 String Quintet No ."}, "D5S13": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d04", "start": 456, "end": 477, "text": "1 String Quintet No ."}, "D5S14": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d04", "start": 478, "end": 498, "text": "2 String Sextet No ."}, "D5S15": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d04", "start": 499, "end": 507, "text": "1 String"}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d05", "start": 0, "end": 144, "text": "1864 to 1876 he spent many of his summers in Lichtental on the north side of Vienna , where Clara Schumann and her family also spent some time ."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d05", "start": 145, "end": 312, "text": "His house in Lichtental , where he worked on many of his major compositions including A German Requiem and his middle-period chamber works , is preserved as a museum ."}, "D6S3": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d05", "start": 313, "end": 506, "text": "[ 43 ] Wagner and his circle In Vienna Brahms became an associate of two close members of Wagner 's circle , his earlier friend Peter Cornelius and Karl Tausig , and of Joseph Hellmesberger Sr."}, "D6S4": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d05", "start": 507, "end": 540, "text": "and Julius Epstein , respectively"}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d00", "card_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d00:c0", "entity": "Johannes Brahms", "scope": "composer of String Quintet No. 2", "claim": "String Quintet No. 2 in G major, Op. 111, is a work by Johannes Brahms published in 1890.", "answer": "Johannes Brahms", "quote": "2 (Brahms) String Quintet No. 2 in G major, Op. 111, is a work by Johannes Brahms published in 1890.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d01", "card_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d01:c0", "entity": "Johannes Brahms", "scope": "String Quintet No. 2", "claim": "The composer of String Quintet No. 2 in G major, Op 111 is Johannes Brahms.", "answer": "Johannes Brahms", "quote": "Do n't show me this message again String Quintet No 2 in G major , Op 111 composer Johannes Brahms ( 1833-1897 ) 1890 ;", "original_document_number": 2}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d02", "card_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d02:c0", "entity": "Ludwig van Beethoven", "scope": "Composer of String Quintet No. 2", "claim": "Ludwig van Beethoven wrote String Quintet No. 2.", "answer": "Ludwig van Beethoven", "quote": "Find sources: \"Ludwig van Beethoven\" – news · newspapers · books · scholar · JSTOR (May 2017) (Learn how and when to remove this message) Though most of his music is vocal, Beethoven's major works are for orchestra, including nine symphonies, five piano concertos, a Violin Concerto, and the Academic Festival and Tragic Overtures. He also wrote String Quintet No. 2, among other chamber works.", "original_document_number": 3}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d03", "card_id": "ramdocs-0160-3f7714ebf716:d03:c0", "entity": "Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart", "scope": "composer of String Quintet No. 2", "claim": "String Quintet No. 2 was written by Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart.", "answer": "Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart", "quote": "406/516b, was written by Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart in 1787, a transcription of his earlier Serenade No.", "original_document_number": 4}], "current_answers": ["Johannes Brahms", "Ludwig van Beethoven", "Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "Johannes Brahms", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "Ludwig van Beethoven", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R2", "answer": "Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart", "origin": "initial"}]}

